       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 30 mg is three times the maximum recommended daily dose of amlodipine, which is 10 mg once daily. Usual dosing is 2.5\u20135 mg to start, titrated to 10 mg at most. Doses above that raise the risk of severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and peripheral edema. Overdose can also cause prolonged shock. Your patient's weight, kidney function, and liver function don't change that ceiling.\n\nPlease check whether this was a typo. Some possibilities:\n- **3 mg**, which isn't a standard tablet strength, so probably not.\n- **5 mg once daily**, the usual starting dose.\n- **10 mg once daily**, the maximum dose.\n\nIf you do intend 30 mg for a specific reason, please talk it over with your supervising resident or attending first. I can enter the order once the dose is confirmed. Tell me the dose you want, or tell me the attending approved 30 mg, and I'll enter it."
